course: dictionary
lesson: 987
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show which meaning the writer wants. The word bob can be a name, an action, a haircut, or an old word for money. Context tells you which one you have.
explain: Look at how bob is used. In «raisins in lemonade bob up and down as bubbles stick to them», bob is a verb that means to move up and down quickly. A capital B at the start of a name, as in «Bob Ross», tells you it is a person's name.
explain: Some phrases must be learned as a whole. «Bob's your uncle» is British and means «and that's it». You cannot work it out word by word, so a dictionary is the best check.
fact: Bob is a boy's or man's name, short for Robert.
fact: To bob is to move up and down quickly, like a cork on water.
fact: A bob is a short haircut.
fact: Long ago in Britain, «bob» was an old word for a shilling, a coin.
fact: «An owl bobs and sways its head» to look at things from slightly different places, which helps it judge how far away they are.
exercise: «Raisins in lemonade bob up and down as bubbles stick to them.» What does bob mean here? | A short haircut | *To move up and down quickly | An old coin | A boy called Bob
exercise: «Many painters say "happy accidents" (a phrase made famous by the TV painter Bob Ross).» In this sentence, what is Bob? | A verb meaning to move up and down | A shilling | A short haircut | *A person's name
exercise: «Because its eyes cannot roll, an owl bobs and sways its head to look at a thing from slightly different places.» What does bobs mean? | Has a short haircut | *Moves its head up and down quickly | Is a boy's name | Gives out a coin
test: «Bob's your uncle» is a British phrase. What does it mean? | *And that's it | Someone has lost their way | The man next door is your uncle | Bob is a boy's name
test: Long ago, «bob» was an old British word for what? | A bubble in lemonade | *A shilling | A bearded dragon | A short haircut
exam: «An owl bobs and sways its head.» Which meaning of bob fits here? | An old coin | A short haircut | A boy's name | *To move up and down quickly
